      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Assume JSON over HTTP: POST /events accepts {\"seats\": positive integer} and returns {\"id\": string, \"seats\": integer, \"remaining\": integer}; POST /events/{id}/reservations accepts an empty JSON object and reserves one seat, returning {\"event_id\": string, \"remaining\": integer}. Errors have shape {\"error\": string}. Discovery must check the environment for existing interface conventions before these defaults are used."
    },
    {
      "id": "K3.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Assume 201 for successful creation or reservation, 400 for invalid JSON or input, 404 for an unknown event, 409 when no seats remain, and 405 for an unsupported method. Unexpected server failures use 500."
    },
    {
      "id": "K4.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "An event starts with a positive whole-number seat capacity; each successful reservation consumes one seat, and availability cannot fall below zero. Reservations stop succeeding when the event is full. Multiple reservations by the same anonymous caller are allowed."
    },
    {
      "id": "K4.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Malformed JSON, missing or extra fields, non-integer or boolean capacities, capacities below one, and reservation bodies other than an empty object are invalid."
    },
    {
      "id": "K5.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "The service process owns event identifiers, capacities, and remaining-seat counts in shared in-memory state for its lifetime; a restart clears them. This rules out durable storage and sharing across multiple service processes."
    },
    {
      "id": "K5.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Assume anonymous callers and no per-person private state or access controls; anyone with access to the service can use its endpoints. Reservation updates must be atomic within one process so concurrent requests cannot overbook. Restart clears all state."
    },
    {
      "id": "K6.1",
      "basis": "inspect",
      "answer": "Use an available Python 3 runtime; discovery must establish the available version and any workspace constraints before selecting a minimum version."
    },
